---
import MainLayout from '../components/MainLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;
---
<MainLayout title="Designing the question">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">01 / Research process</p>
    <h1>Designing the question<span>.</span></h1>
    <p class="intro">A space to trace the path from an initial curiosity to a focused research question. The direction can change as new ideas, references and observations emerge.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="entry-list">
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">01 / Starting point</p>
      <h2>What is drawing my attention?</h2>
      <p class="muted">Collect the interests, experiences or observations that make this subject worth exploring. What feels unresolved or keeps coming back?</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">02 / Exploring the subject</p>
      <h2>What do I want to understand?</h2>
      <p class="muted">Note questions, tensions and possible directions. Which parts feel most specific, meaningful or open to investigation?</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">03 / Shaping the question</p>
      <h2>What could I investigate?</h2>
      <p class="muted">Try working versions of the research question. Keep track of what each version includes, leaves out and makes possible.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="eyebrow">04 / Next steps</p>
      <h2>What should I follow up?</h2>
      <p class="muted">List the conversations, readings, references or experiments that could help clarify the direction.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <section class="section-block">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Continue exploring</p>
      <a href={`${base}notes/`}>Open all notes ↗</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Use the notebook to collect dated observations and reflections as the research question develops.</p>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
